    pr_ref:  # 1c4d
    description: "**Problem.** When `--backend rust-analyzer` is selected but rust-analyzer crashes mid-run (most commonly SIGKILL'd by the OOM-killer on memory-pressured large crates), the graceful-degrade path swaps in tree-sitter output without telling the user. Exit code 0; stderr empty; analysis \"completes.\" The user has no way to know their requested backend silently fell through.\n\n**Concrete trigger** (diagnosed 2026-05-10, see `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05102026_0400.md` §3):\n\n- wasmtime (570K LOC, ~80 crates, heavy Cranelift macros + component-model bindings) + `--backend rust-analyzer` on a 22 GiB box with ~17 GiB free at run-start.\n- `rust-analyzer scip` routinely needs 16-32 GiB+ on wasmtime-class workspaces.\n- SIGKILL → returncode `-9` / `137` → routes to `RustAnalyzerInvocationFailed` → graceful-degrade catches it → tree-sitter output substituted silently.\n- 600s wrapper timeout was not reached (300s wall), so the timeout path didn't fire.\n- 5.0.1-era `rust-analyzer --version` binary smoke-test passes; the failure is at the analysis-artifact layer, not the binary layer.\n\n**Diagnostic signature.** When the backend silently falls through, the resulting behavior map has:\n- Every edge attributed to `origin=\"rust-v1\"` (the tree-sitter origin).\n- Zero edges with `origin=\"scip\"`.\n- On a repo containing `.rs` files (so SCIP output was expected).\n\nThat's the assertion to wire as the artifact-level engagement check.\n\n**Why this matters beyond wasmtime.**\n\n1. **It already invalidated diagnostic work upstream.** WI-mirus-pupas (filed April; closed wont_do 2026-05-17) asked \"is it worth re-testing procMacro.enable on heavier crates?\" The original WI-ronot ripgrep test got \"byte-identical SCIP symbol set when toggling procMacro flags\" — but we now have no way to know whether rust-analyzer engaged on either run, so the result tells us nothing. The May 10 silent-fall-through finding is what surfaced this.\n\n2. **The May 10 journal recorded \"Decision: not filing as a tracker item\"** based on the assumption the trigger is uncommon (wasmtime-class repo + <32 GiB RAM). That assessment was made before WI-mirus-pupas's premise collapsed. We now have two distinct downstream impacts (wasmtime test invalidated, WI-mirus-pupas premise invalidated), which moves this from \"rare edge case\" to \"load-bearing diagnostic gap.\"\n\n**Fix proposal (small, structural).**\n\n1. **Surface the exit code + stderr tail in the graceful-degrade path** when `--backend rust-analyzer` was explicitly requested. The user asked for a specific backend; they deserve to know when their analysis silently degraded.\n\n2. **If returncode is `-9` / `137`, hint at memory exhaustion explicitly.** Suggested message: \"rust-analyzer was SIGKILL'd (likely OOM). This crate may need >16 GiB RAM. Falling back to tree-sitter.\"\n\n3. **Artifact-level engagement check.** Post-run, if a `--backend rust-analyzer` invocation produced zero `origin=\"scip\"` edges on a repo containing `.rs` files, surface a warning. This catches the case where rust-analyzer \"succeeded\" (exit 0) but produced no SCIP output for some other reason.\n\n**Test coverage.**\n\n- Mock rust-analyzer wrapper raising `RustAnalyzerInvocationFailed` with returncode=-9; assert the user-facing message contains the OOM hint.\n- Mock rust-analyzer wrapper returning empty SCIP output; assert the post-run engagement-check warning fires when `.rs` files are present.\n\n**Related.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/src/hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer/invoke.py` — exception classes already carry stderr/exit_code; the swallowing happens at the orchestrator's graceful-degrade catch.\n- WI-nohah (closed 2026-04-XX) — original graceful-degrade implementation; this item extends its diagnostics, not its degrade behavior.\n- v5.0.1 release added `rust-analyzer --version` exit-code smoke-test (the prior layer of the engagement-check ladder); this item is the next layer down (artifact engagement).\n- WI-mirus-pupas (closed wont_do 2026-05-17) — its premise was invalidated by this bug."  # 1c4d
